<title>HONG KONG: Tommy Hilfiger to expand in Europe.</title>
<headline>Tommy Hilfiger to expand in Europe.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tommy Hilfiger Corp on Wednesday said it entered into a licensing arrangement with Pepe Jeans London Corp to distribute its products in Europe.</p>
<p>&quot;Europe presents a tremendous opportunity for expanding our business,&quot; it said. &quot;By partnering with Pepe, one of the few truly pan-European companies, we can immediately seize and capitalize on this expansion opportunity.&quot;</p>
<p>Tommy Hilfiger said it planned to sell its men's sportswear in leading department and specialty stores in London, Paris, Madrid and Dusseldorf in the fall of 1997, with plans to open regional showrooms across the continent.</p>
</text>
